+# Pre-Ship Review — USDC Payouts dApp (Base)
+
+Reviewer pass over `packages/nextjs` + configuration, against the SE-2 pre-ship QA checklist.
+Scope: report only, no code changed.
+
+**Verdict: do not ship.** 8 ship-blocking issues, 19 should-fix. The most serious is that the
+address the frontend transacts against has no code on Base mainnet.
+
+---
+
+## Ship-blocking
+
+### 1. The Payouts contract is not deployed at the address the app uses
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts:10` (`0x7c3f2A9d41B85E60Cf14a14e2b9D073A55e0b6F2`)
+
+Verified live against Base mainnet:
+```
+eth_getCode(0x7c3f...b6F2) -> "0x"      # no contract
+eth_getBalance(0x7c3f...b6F2) -> 0x0    # never used
+eth_getCode(0x8335...2913) -> "0x6080…" # USDC is real, so the RPC call is sound
+```
+Every `pay()` call from the UI will be a value-less call to an EOA: it silently "succeeds" on
+chain, no transfer happens, no `Paid` event is emitted, and the user's approval is left standing
+to an address nobody controls. The event feed will stay permanently empty.
+
+**Fix:** redeploy (`yarn deploy --network base`), let the deploy step regenerate
+`deployedContracts.ts`, and confirm `eth_getCode` is non-empty before shipping. Do not hand-edit
+the address.
+
+### 2. Contract is not verified on Basescan
+**File:** same as above
+
+Cannot be verified — there is nothing there to verify. After the redeploy in #1, run
+`yarn verify --network base` and confirm the green checkmark on basescan.org. Also replace the
+shared default key in `packages/hardhat/hardhat.config.ts:17`
+(`ETHERSCAN_API_KEY || "DNXJA8RX2Q3VZ4URQIWP7Z68CJXQZSC6AW"`) with the team's own key.
+
+### 3. Disconnected state is a sentence, not a Connect button
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:70-71`
+```tsx
+{!isConnected ? (
+  <p className="mt-4">Please connect your wallet to send a payout.</p>
+```
+The primary CTA slot on the page's main flow is a paragraph. The only way to connect is the small
+header button.
+
+**Fix:** render the connect button in the CTA slot:
+```tsx
+import { RainbowKitCustomConnectButton } from "~~/components/scaffold-eth";
+...
+{!isConnected ? <RainbowKitCustomConnectButton /> : ( ... )}
+```
+
+### 4. No network check — wrong-chain users transact into the void
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:21, 36-62`
+
+`useWriteContract()` is called with no `chainId`, so wagmi submits to whatever chain the wallet is
+currently on. A user on Ethereum mainnet clicking **Approve** sends an `approve` to
+`0x8335…2913` on mainnet — a different contract entirely. The header `WrongNetworkDropdown` is not
+sufficient; the action button itself must become the switch CTA.
+
+**Fix:** branch the CTA slot:
+```tsx
+const chainId = useChainId();
+const { switchChain } = useSwitchChain();
+if (chainId !== targetNetwork.id)
+  return <button className="btn btn-primary" onClick={() => switchChain({ chainId: targetNetwork.id })}>
+    Switch to {targetNetwork.name}
+  </button>;
+```
+Also pass `chainId: targetNetwork.id` on every write as a backstop.
+
+### 5. Raw wagmi `useWriteContract` instead of `useScaffoldWriteContract`
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:6, 21`
+
+`isPending` from raw wagmi flips back to `false` the moment the wallet returns a tx hash — not when
+the transaction confirms. Both buttons re-enable mid-flight, and there is no tx toast, no block
+confirmation wait, and no `getParsedError` handling. AGENTS.md requires the scaffold hooks.
+
+**Fix:**
+```tsx
+const { writeContractAsync: payWrite, isPending } = useScaffoldWriteContract({ contractName: "Payouts" });
+const { writeContractAsync: usdcWrite } = useScaffoldWriteContract({ contractName: "USDC" });
+await payWrite({ functionName: "pay", args: [recipient, parseUnits(amount, 6), memo] });
+```
+This also removes the direct `deployedContracts` import at line 7.
+
+### 6. Approve and Send Payout are both visible, with no allowance check
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:99-114`
+
+Both buttons render side by side at all times. There is no `allowance` read (the ABI has it —
+`deployedContracts.ts:71`), so the app cannot know which step the user is on. A user who clicks
+**Send Payout** first eats a revert on `transferFrom`; a user who has already approved is still
+shown **Approve**.
+
+**Fix:** read allowance and render exactly one button:
+```tsx
+const { data: allowance, refetch: refetchAllowance } = useScaffoldReadContract({
+  contractName: "USDC", functionName: "allowance",
+  args: [connectedAddress, PAYOUTS_ADDRESS],
+});
+const needsApproval = (allowance ?? 0n) < parseUnits(amount || "0", 6);
+```
+then `{needsApproval ? <ApproveButton/> : <PayButton/>}`.
+
+### 7. Double-submit window on Approve
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:100-106`
+
+`disabled={isPending}` is the only guard, and it is the *same* `isPending` shared by both buttons.
+Between wallet-signature and block-confirmation, and again between confirmation and allowance cache
+refresh, the button is live. Users will approve twice and pay gas twice.
+
+**Fix:** the two-state lock from the QA checklist:
+```tsx
+const [approvalSubmitting, setApprovalSubmitting] = useState(false);
+const [approveCooldown, setApproveCooldown] = useState(false);
+
+const handleApprove = async () => {
+  if (approvalSubmitting || approveCooldown) return;
+  setApprovalSubmitting(true);
+  try {
+    await usdcWrite({ functionName: "approve", args: [PAYOUTS_ADDRESS, parseUnits(amount, 6)] });
+    setApproveCooldown(true);
+    setTimeout(() => { setApproveCooldown(false); refetchAllowance(); }, 4000);
+  } catch (e) {
+    notification.error(getParsedError(e));
+  } finally {
+    setApprovalSubmitting(false);   // must be finally — releases on user rejection too
+  }
+};
+<button disabled={isPending || approvalSubmitting || approveCooldown}>
+```
+
+### 8. All errors are swallowed to the console
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:44-46, 59-61`
+```tsx
+} catch (e) {
+  console.error(e);
+}
+```
+Every failure mode — user rejection, insufficient balance, `Payouts: zero amount`,
+`Payouts: zero recipient`, `Payouts: transfer failed`, wrong chain — produces zero UI feedback. The
+button just re-enables and the user assumes the app is broken.
+
+**Fix:**
+```tsx
+import { getParsedError, notification } from "~~/utils/scaffold-eth";
+...
+} catch (e) { notification.error(getParsedError(e)); }
+```
+`useScaffoldWriteContract` (#5) also surfaces tx toasts automatically.
+
+### 9. SE-2 template branding is still everywhere
+Users will see a payouts app that claims to be Scaffold-ETH.
+
+| Where | Line | Current |
+|---|---|---|
+| `packages/nextjs/app/layout.tsx` | 11-12 | `title: 'Scaffold-ETH 2 App'`, `description: 'Built with 🏗 Scaffold-ETH 2'` |
+| `packages/nextjs/utils/scaffold-eth/getMetadata.ts` | 8 | `titleTemplate = "%s \| Scaffold-ETH 2"` |
+| `packages/nextjs/components/Header.tsx` | 90-98 | "SE2 logo", "Scaffold-ETH / Ethereum dev stack" brand block |
+| `packages/nextjs/components/Footer.tsx` | 46-77 | "Fork me" → scaffold-eth repo, "Built with ❤ at BuidlGuidl", SE-2 Telegram "Support" link |
+| `packages/nextjs/app/page.tsx` | 21-40 | "Welcome to Scaffold-ETH 2", "Get started by editing packages/nextjs/app/page.tsx", `YourContract.sol` |
+| `README.md` | 1-20 | Unmodified SE-2 template README |
+| `packages/nextjs/public/manifest.json` | 2-3 | `'Scaffold-ETH 2 DApp'` |
+| `packages/nextjs/public/favicon.png`, `thumbnail.jpg` | — | Stock SE-2 assets |
+
+**Fix:** title/description → "USDC Payouts"; drop `titleTemplate` or make it `%s | USDC Payouts`;
+replace the Footer link row with the team's repo (keep `SwitchTheme`, drop `BuidlGuidlLogo`);
+rewrite the home page as a real landing page (or redirect `/` → `/payouts`); rewrite README for this
+project; swap favicon and OG thumbnail.
+
+---
+
+## Should-fix
+
+### 10. `pollingInterval: 30000` on an L2
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/scaffold.config.ts:24` — Base blocks every 2s; a 30s poll makes the
+balance and payout feed look frozen after a successful tx. Set to `3000`.
+
+### 11. Shipping with the shared default Alchemy key and WalletConnect project ID
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/scaffold.config.ts:29, 40`, `rpcOverrides` empty at 32-35.
+`NEXT_PUBLIC_ALCHEMY_API_KEY` and `NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLET_CONNECT_PROJECT_ID` are referenced but there
+is no `.env.local` here and nothing confirms they are set on the host. Under the default key you
+share a rate limit with every SE-2 project on the internet.
+
+**Fix:** get project-owned keys, add
+`rpcOverrides: { [chains.base.id]: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_RPC_URL }`, then confirm on the
+host (`vercel env ls | grep -i "RPC\|ALCHEMY\|WALLET_CONNECT"`) — referencing `process.env` is not
+the same as setting it.
+
+### 12. Bare `http()` fallback transport still in the wagmi config
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/services/web3/wagmiConfig.tsx:20` — `rpcFallbacks` always ends with a
+bare `http()`, which resolves to the public `mainnet.base.org` endpoint and will rate-limit under
+real traffic. Remove the bare `http()` once a real RPC override (#11) is configured.
+
+### 13. Recipient uses a raw `<input type="text">`
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:78-84` — no ENS resolution, no checksum validation,
+no blockie preview. The value is cast straight to `0x${string}` at line 55, so a typo'd or truncated
+address becomes a failed tx (or, if it happens to be valid, an unrecoverable payout to a stranger).
+
+**Fix:** `import { AddressInput } from "@scaffold-ui/components";` →
+`<AddressInput value={recipient} onChange={setRecipient} placeholder="0x... or ENS name" />`, and
+gate the pay button on `isAddress(recipient)`.
+
+### 14. The Payouts contract address is never shown
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx` (whole page) — users are approving USDC spend to a
+contract they cannot see or inspect. Render it near the form with
+`<Address address={PAYOUTS.address} chain={targetNetwork} />` for the blockie, copy button, and
+Basescan link.
+
+### 15. Feed addresses use a hand-rolled `shorten()` instead of `<Address/>`
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:13, 122, 124` — loses ENS names, blockies, copy, and
+explorer links. Replace both spans with `<Address address={payout.args.from} chain={targetNetwork} />`.
+
+### 16. No USD values anywhere
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:75, 87, 126` — USDC is dollar-pegged, so the fix is
+cheap: render the balance and the feed amounts formatted as currency (`$1,250.00`) rather than a
+bare `1250 USDC`, and echo the dollar value under the amount input as the user types.
+
+### 17. Event history scans from block 0
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:32` — `fromBlock: 0n` on Base mainnet means ~36M
+blocks of `eth_getLogs`, which every provider will reject or throttle; combined with `watch: true`
+it re-runs continuously. `deployedContracts.ts:48` already records `deployedOnBlock: 33712450`.
+
+**Fix:** `fromBlock: BigInt(deployedContracts[8453].Payouts.deployedOnBlock)`.
+
+### 18. USDC was hand-added to `deployedContracts.ts`
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts:50` — that file is autogenerated (see its
+own header comment) and only `Payouts` is in `packages/hardhat/deploy/00_deploy_payouts.ts`. The
+next `yarn deploy` wipes the USDC entry and the page breaks.
+`packages/nextjs/contracts/externalContracts.ts:14` is empty.
+
+**Fix:** move the USDC block into `externalContracts.ts` under key `8453`.
+
+### 19. Hardcoded dark background breaks the theme system
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:65` — `bg-black text-white` (and `border-gray-700`
+at line 121) bypasses DaisyUI entirely. The `SwitchTheme` toggle in the footer does nothing on this
+page, and light-mode users get a black page inside a light header/footer.
+
+**Fix:** `<div className="min-h-screen bg-base-200 text-base-content">` and `border-base-300`.
+
+### 20. DaisyUI `loading` class applied to the buttons
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:101, 108` — `${isPending ? "loading" : ""}` on a
+`btn` replaces the whole label with a full-size spinner; the button looks broken and the text
+vanishes.
+
+**Fix:**
+```tsx
+<button className="btn btn-primary" disabled={...}>
+  {isPending && <span className="loading loading-spinner loading-sm mr-2" />}
+  {isPending ? "Approving..." : "Approve"}
+</button>
+```
+
+### 21. `--radius-field: 9999rem` makes the memo textarea a pill
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/styles/globals.css:36` and `:63` — the multi-line memo textarea at
+`app/payouts/page.tsx:92-97` renders with fully rounded ends and clips text at the corners. Set
+`--radius-field: 0.5rem;` in **both** `@plugin "daisyui/theme"` blocks — do not patch with
+per-component `rounded-*` classes.
+
+### 22. Phantom is missing from the wallet list
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/services/web3/wagmiConnectors.tsx:20-28` — add `phantomWallet` to the
+`wallets` array (import from `@rainbow-me/rainbowkit/wallets`). A meaningful share of users cannot
+connect today.
+
+### 23. No mobile deep-linking on any transaction button
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:36-62` — RainbowKit v2 / WalletConnect v2 does not
+auto-open the wallet app. A mobile user taps Approve and nothing visible happens; they must
+manually switch apps and hope a push arrived.
+
+**Fix:** a `writeAndOpen` helper wrapping **both** writes — fire the write first, then
+`setTimeout(openWallet, 2000)`. `openWallet` must skip when `window.ethereum` exists (already inside
+a wallet browser) and must pick the scheme from the WalletConnect session in `localStorage`
+(`wc@2:client…`) plus `wagmi.recentConnectorId`, since `connector.id` only ever says
+`"walletConnect"`.
+
+### 24. OG image falls back to a localhost URL
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/utils/scaffold-eth/getMetadata.ts:5-7, 19` — if
+`VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL` is not set in the build environment, every OG/Twitter card points at
+`http://localhost:3000/thumbnail.jpg` and unfurls as a broken image everywhere the app is shared.
+
+**Fix:** set an explicit `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL` and use it as the base, failing the build (or at
+least warning loudly) if it is missing in production.
+
+### 25. `manifest.json` is not valid JSON
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/public/manifest.json:2-4` — unquoted keys and single-quoted strings; any
+parser rejects it. It is also not linked from `layout.tsx`, so it is currently dead weight either
+way. Either fix it to real JSON with the project's own name/icons and add
+`<link rel="manifest">`, or delete the file.
+
+### 26. WalletConnect app name is `scaffold-eth-2`
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/services/web3/wagmiConnectors.tsx:49` — this string is what shows in the
+wallet's connection-approval sheet. Users approving a payout app see "scaffold-eth-2". Set it to the
+product name.
+
+### 27. Debug Contracts is in the production nav
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/components/Header.tsx:30-31` — a raw ABI console pointed at a mainnet
+contract, shipped to end users. Remove the link (and ideally the route) for the production build, or
+gate it on `targetNetwork.id === hardhat.id` the way the Faucet and Block Explorer links already are.
+
+### 28. No client-side validation before submitting
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:49-62` — `amount` empty coerces to `parseUnits("0")`
+and reverts on `Payouts: zero amount` (line 22 of `Payouts.sol`); an amount over the user's balance
+reverts inside `transferFrom`; an empty `recipient` reverts on `Payouts: zero recipient`. All three
+cost gas and, per #8, show nothing.
+
+**Fix:** disable the pay button unless `isAddress(recipient)`, `parsedAmount > 0n`, and
+`parsedAmount <= usdcBalance`; show the reason inline.
+
+### 29. Approval amount goes stale
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:42` — approval is for exactly `amount` at click
+time. If the user raises the amount after approving, the pay call reverts with no explanation.
+Re-deriving `needsApproval` from the live allowance (#6) covers this; approving `maxUint256` (with
+the tradeoff stated in the UI) is the other option.

